# Approver identity for the quantum-job CI/CD pipeline (see
# qiskit-runtime/WORKFLOWS.md's accountability model, and the paper at
# doc/running-quantum-jobs-in-cicd.md, Part 5).
#
# This file, not just the prod GitHub Environment's required-reviewer
# setting, is the durable record of who is accountable for vouching for a
# circuit change: it's checked into the repo, its own edits go through PR
# review, and every approval it requires shows up directly in the PR's
# review history -- discoverable by anyone reading the PR, not just someone
# with access to Settings -> Environments. The environment's required
# reviewers remain a separate, additional gate at RUN time (approving that
# THIS specific execution should spend money right now); this file gates
# MERGE time (approving that this specific diff is sound). Keep both --
# they answer different questions.
#
# Update the owner below to reflect whoever is actually quantum-literate
# and accountable for this pipeline as the team grows; a single owner
# doesn't scale past one person's availability.
/qiskit-runtime/circuits/   @dreads
/qiskit-runtime/payload.py  @dreads
/qiskit-runtime/submit.py   @dreads
/qiskit-runtime/run.py      @dreads
